  "articleHtml": "<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Chicken Breast Nutrition Facts\n    </span>\n</p>\n<div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Chicken breast stands out for one simple reason: it provides a large amount of protein without bringing along much carbohydrate or fat.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     A\n    </span>\n<span>\n     100g serving of cooked, roasted chicken breast contains about 165 calories and 31g of protein\n    </span>\n<span>\n     . It also provides around 3.6g of fat and virtually no carbohydrates, making protein the dominant macronutrient in its nutrition profile.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.hw45urtklsxb\">\n<span>\n     100g of Chicken Breast at a Glance\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<div>\n<div><div><div><div class=\"overflow-x-auto my-6 rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 glass-card-static\"><table class=\"w-full text-left border-collapse\">\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Nutrient\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Amount\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Calories\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         165 kcal\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Protein\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         31 g\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Total Fat\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         3.6 g\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Carbohydrates\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         0 g\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Dietary Fiber\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         0 g\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Total Sugars\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         0 g\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Cholesterol\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         85 mg\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Sodium\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         74 mg\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Potassium\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         256 mg\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Calcium\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         15 mg\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         Iron\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-sm text-zinc-300 border-b border-zinc-800/50\" colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\">\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n         1 mg\n        </span>\n</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div></div></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     These values refer to\n    </span>\n<span>\n     cooked, roasted chicken breast meat without skin\n    </span>\n<span>\n     .\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.w28es94a6bn\">\n<span>\n     Why Chicken Breast Is So Protein-Dense\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     With approximately\n    </span>\n<span>\n     31g of protein for 165 calories\n    </span>\n<span>\n     , chicken breast provides a substantial amount of protein relative to its calorie content.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Protein accounts for most of the energy in this food, while fat contributes a much smaller share and carbohydrates contribute essentially none.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     This nutritional balance is why chicken breast frequently appears in meals built around a specific protein target.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If you are trying to estimate how much protein you need in a full day, NutritionSolver's\n    </span>\n<span>\n     Protein Calculator\n    </span>\n<span>\n     can provide a personalized starting estimate.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.j6zp1ypgvk8y\">\n<span>\n     Does Chicken Breast Have Carbs?\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Plain chicken breast naturally contains virtually\n    </span>\n<span>\n     zero carbohydrates\n    </span>\n<span>\n     .\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     This also means it contains no meaningful dietary fiber or sugar on its own.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     The nutrition profile can change once chicken is breaded, glazed, marinated, coated in sauce, or prepared with carbohydrate-containing ingredients. If you are checking nutrition for a prepared chicken dish, the complete recipe matters more than the chicken alone.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.hdzrhyz5w4ea\">\n<span>\n     How Much Fat Is in Chicken Breast?\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Cooked skinless chicken breast contains approximately\n    </span>\n<span>\n     3.6g of total fat per 100g\n    </span>\n<span>\n     .\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Removing the skin keeps the fat content much lower than many skin-on chicken preparations. Cooking oil, butter, sauces, and marinades can add additional fat and calories, so the nutrition of a finished meal may differ considerably from the plain chicken values shown here.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.bfkkxpu96wa0\">\n<span>\n     Why Cooked and Raw Chicken Breast Have Different Calories per 100g\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     This is one of the most important details when reading chicken nutrition data.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     The\n    </span>\n<span>\n     165 calories and 31g of protein shown here refer to cooked chicken breast\n    </span>\n<span>\n     .\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Chicken loses water as it cooks. Because the cooked meat contains less water, protein and calories become more concentrated in every 100 grams.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     That means 100g of raw chicken and 100g of cooked chicken should not be treated as nutritionally identical, even when they came from the same piece of meat.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For accurate food tracking, use nutrition data that matches the state in which you weigh the chicken:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Weighed raw \u2192 use raw chicken nutrition data\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Weighed cooked \u2192 use cooked chicken nutrition data\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.ke3i4flkwq0p\">\n<span>\n     What Does a Larger Portion Provide?\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     The values on this page are standardized to 100g, but your actual portion may be larger or smaller.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For example, increasing the amount of plain cooked chicken breast will increase calories and protein in roughly the same proportion. A portion weighing twice as much as the 100g reference will contain roughly twice the listed nutrients.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Using grams is useful because chicken breasts vary considerably in size, so \u201cone chicken breast\u201d is not a consistent serving measurement.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.kjqwvtkod5dy\">\n<span>\n     Common Chicken Breast Nutrition Questions\n    </span>\n</h2><div class=\"faq-accordion-container space-y-3 my-6\"><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>How much protein is in 100g of chicken breast?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>How many calories are in 100g of chicken breast?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Is chicken breast high in protein?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Why does cooked chicken have more protein per 100g than raw chicken?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details></div>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.b3s8mzwc7khr\">\n<span>\n     Nutrition Data Reference\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     NutritionSolver presents values for\n    </span>\n<span>\n     cooked, roasted chicken breast meat per 100g\n    </span>\n<span>\n     using USDA food composition reference data.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Actual values can vary depending on the cut, cooking method, moisture loss, added ingredients, and whether the skin is included.\n    </span>\n</p>",
  "seoTitle": "Chicken Breast Nutrition Facts: Calories & Protein",
  "seoDescription": "See chicken breast nutrition facts per 100g, including 165 calories, 31g protein, fat, carbs, potassium, sodium, and other key nutrients."
